speechtext:
I wish to say just a word or two in connection with dredges, and perhaps I should have brought this up under 299. Members from British, Columbia referred to the condition of dredges on the Pacific coast;
(Mr. MacNiool.l
I wish to discuss the dredges on the Atlantic coast and make a requisition for some money for the provision of new equipment in that part of the country. There are plenty of dredges there now, but their condition is simply terrible and it is time we got new equipment. Dredges cannot be built' overnight, and money ought to be appropriated now for the purpose so that we may have suitable dredges of light, medium and heavy type. The department informs me that there are dredges there, but no dredges are available for the kind of work needed, and as I say, they cannot be obtained at a moment's notice.
